msgid "Authorize access to web endpoints"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To control which callers can access the web endpoints of a {project-name} application, define authorization rules with security annotations or HTTP security policies for request paths.\n"
"When security is active, {project-name} checks every HTTP request against these rules to determine whether it can proceed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most authorization rules check the roles and permissions of the `SecurityIdentity` that represents the caller.\n"
"The security identity provider supplies the roles.\n"
"To customize them, create a `SecurityIdentityAugmentor`, as described in xref:security-customization.adoc#security-identity-customization[Security Identity Customization]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Authorize requests in configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To protect paths without a change to the code, define HTTP permissions in the `application.properties` file.\n"
"Each permission set names paths, optionally HTTP methods, and the policy that decides whether a request to those paths can proceed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Be careful when you create complex, possibly overlapping HTTP security policy path expressions.\n"
"Make sure that there are no typos in the configured policy paths.\n"
"Be aware that the root path is only prepended to the policy paths that do not start with a forward slash, for more information, see the <<permission-paths-and-root-paths>> section.\n"
"Test your HTTP policy configuration thoroughly, verify that the allowed requests succeed and that the requests with invalid credentials or\n"
"insufficient permissions are rejected.\n"
"If you work with Jakarta RESTful Web Services (Jakarta REST) endpoints, prefer <<standard-security-annotations,standard security annotations>> to the path-based HTTP security policies."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you work with Jakarta REST endpoints and need to set default security requirements, prefer using <<standard-security-annotations,standard security annotations>> and the `quarkus.security.jaxrs.deny-unannotated-endpoints` or `quarkus.security.jaxrs.default-roles-allowed` property instead of HTTP security policy path matching, see <<configuration-properties-to-deny-access>>.\n"
"Security annotations can override these properties on an individual Jakarta REST resource or method."
msgstr ""

msgid "A permission set can use a built-in policy:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus built-in policies"
msgstr ""

msgid "Built-in policy"
msgstr "組込ポリシー"

msgid "Description"
msgstr "説明"

msgid "`deny`"
msgstr "`deny`"

msgid "This policy denies all users."
msgstr "このポリシーは、すべてのユーザーを拒否します。"

msgid "`permit`"
msgstr "`permit`"

msgid "This policy permits all users."
msgstr "このポリシーは、すべてのユーザーを許可します。"

msgid "`authenticated`"
msgstr "`authenticated`"

msgid "This policy permits only authenticated users."
msgstr "このポリシーは、認証されたユーザーのみを許可します。"

msgid "A permission set can also use a role-based policy that you define, which allows users with specific roles to access the resources:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This defines a role-based policy that allows users with the `user` role or the `admin` role."
msgstr ""

msgid "To apply the policies, reference them from permission sets in the `application.properties` file:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This permission references the built-in `permit` policy to allow `GET` requests to `/public` and its sub-paths.\n"
"Because the permission lists only `GET`, requests with other methods to the same paths are denied."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This permission references the built-in `deny` policy for both `/forbidden` and `/forbidden/` paths.\n"
"It is an exact path match because it does not end with `*`."
msgstr ""
"この権限は、 `/forbidden` パスと `/forbidden/` パスの両方に対して組み込みの `deny` ポリシーを参照します。\n"
"これは `*` で終わっていないため、パスが完マッチします。"

msgid ""
"This permission set references the `role-policy1` policy.\n"
"`roles1` is an example name; you can call the permission sets whatever you want."
msgstr ""

msgid "With this configuration, an anonymous request to `/api/orders` is rejected with the challenge of the configured authentication mechanism, for example, the HTTP 401 status for Basic authentication, and a request from an authenticated caller that has neither the `user` role nor the `admin` role gets the HTTP 403 status."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The exact path pattern `/forbidden` also secures the `/forbidden/` path.\n"
"This matters because a Jakarta REST endpoint answers both paths, so both paths need to be secured to secure the endpoint.\n"
"For example, the `deny1` permission secures the `forbidden` endpoint of this resource:"
msgstr ""

msgid "To permit access to the `/forbidden/` path only, add a permission with that more specific exact path:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `/forbidden/` path is not secured, while the `/forbidden` path stays denied."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A permission set can list several paths and several methods, separated by commas.\n"
"When several permission sets match a request, {project-name} chooses between them as described in <<path-matching-rules>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A configured HTTP security policy must not contain a semicolon `;` character in its `paths` property.\n"
"Use a <<custom-http-security-policy,custom HTTP security policy>> when a security policy decision depends on the presence of certain matrix parameters in the request path."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write a custom HTTP security policy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When an authorization decision depends on the request itself, implement the `io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.security.HttpSecurityPolicy` interface in an application-scoped CDI bean.\n"
"A named policy applies only where you assign it.\n"
"A nameless policy is a global policy, as described later in this section."
msgstr ""

msgid "Named HTTP Security policy will only be applied to the requests that you assign it to, for example, with the `application.properties` path matching rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "To assign the named policy to paths, reference it from a permission set:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Custom policy name must match the value returned by the `io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.security.HttpSecurityPolicy.name` method."
msgstr "カスタムポリシー名は、 `io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.security.HttpSecurityPolicy.name` メソッドによって返される値とマッチする必要があります。"

msgid "Alternatively, bind the named policy to Jakarta REST endpoints with the `@AuthorizationPolicy` security annotation:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@AuthorizationPolicy` annotation can be used together with other standard security annotations.\n"
"As usual, the method-level annotation has priority over class-level annotation."
msgstr ""
"`@AuthorizationPolicy` アノテーションは、他の標準セキュリティーアノテーションと合わせて使用できます。\n"
"通常どおり、メソッドレベルのアノテーションはクラスレベルのアノテーションよりも優先されます。"

msgid "Apply custom named HttpSecurityPolicy to the Jakarta REST `hello` endpoint."
msgstr "カスタム名の HttpSecurityPolicy を Jakarta REST `hello` エンドポイントに適用します。"

msgid ""
"The `@AuthorizationPolicy` annotation binds only policies that are CDI beans, such as `CustomNamedHttpSecPolicy`.\n"
"It cannot bind a role-based policy that you define with `quarkus.http.auth.policy.` properties."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create a global `HttpSecurityPolicy`, do not implement the `io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.security.HttpSecurityPolicy.name` method and leave the policy nameless.\n"
"When {project-name} authorizes a request to the main HTTP server, it runs every global policy in addition to the permission sets that match the request.\n"
"The management interface authorizes its requests with the named policies of its own `quarkus.management.auth.permission` properties, as described in xref:management-interface-reference.adoc#use-http-security-policy-to-enable-path-based-authentication[Use HTTP Security Policy to enable path-based authentication]."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Inject <code>@RequestScoped</code> beans into <code>HttpSecurityPolicy</code>"
msgstr "<code>@RequestScoped</code> ビーンを <code>HttpSecurityPolicy</code> に注入します"

msgid ""
"A policy can inject `@RequestScoped` beans only when the xref:cdi-reference.adoc#request-context-lifecycle[CDI request context] is active and the beans are prepared.\n"
"You can activate the context yourself, for example, with the `@ActivateRequestContext` annotation.\n"
"However, authorization happens before Quarkus prepares some `@RequestScoped` beans, such as the Jakarta REST `jakarta.ws.rs.core.UriInfo` bean."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Instead of activating the context yourself, apply the `HttpSecurityPolicy` to Jakarta REST endpoints.\n"
"{project-name} then activates and prepares the CDI request context for you.\n"
"Use one of the following ways:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the `@AuthorizationPolicy` security annotation."
msgstr "`@AuthorizationPolicy` セキュリティーアノテーションを使用します。"

msgid "Call `applyToJaxRs()` on the `HttpSecurity.HttpPermission` when you <<path-specific-authz-programmatic-set-up,define the policy programmatically>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set the `quarkus.http.auth.permission.custom1.applies-to=jaxrs` configuration property.\n"
"With the `jaxrs` value, the permission runs after {project-name} matches the request with a Jakarta REST endpoint.\n"
"The default value is `all`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A permission that applies to Jakarta REST endpoints runs after authentication, so it cannot select an authentication mechanism with the `auth-mechanism` property or the `basic()` method.\n"
"To select the authentication mechanism of a Jakarta REST endpoint, annotate the endpoint, for example, with `@BasicAuthentication`, as described in xref:security-authentication-mechanisms.adoc#use-annotations-for-path-based-auth[Use annotations to enable path-based authentication for Jakarta REST endpoints]."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Map <code>SecurityIdentity</code> roles"
msgstr "Map <code>SecurityIdentity</code> のロール"

msgid ""
"To use deployment-specific role names, map the roles of the `SecurityIdentity` to other roles.\n"
"The mapped roles are then applicable for endpoint authorization by using the `@RolesAllowed` annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role-based policy that wins the path match for a request can map the roles for that request:"
msgstr ""

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Map the `admin` role to the `Admin1` role.\n"
"The `SecurityIdentity` will have both `admin` and `Admin1` roles."
msgstr "`「admin` 」ロールを「 `Admin1` 」ロールにマッピングしてください。 `SecurityIdentity` には、 `「admin` 」ロールと `「Admin1` 」ロールの両方が割り当てられます。"

msgid "The `/*` path is secured, and only authenticated HTTP requests are granted access, because `admin-policy1` does not set the `roles-allowed` property, and its default value, `+**+`, allows any authenticated user."
msgstr ""

msgid "To map the `SecurityIdentity` roles to the deployment-specific roles regardless of a path, use the `quarkus.http.auth.roles-mapping` property:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `/*` path is not secured.\n"
"You must secure your endpoints with standard security annotations or define HTTP permissions in addition to this configuration property."
msgstr "`/*` パスは保護されていません。標準のセキュリティーアノテーションを使用してエンドポイントを保護するか、この設定プロパティーに加えて HTTP 権限を定義する必要があります。"

msgid "To add the same mapping programmatically, observe the `io.quarkus.vertx.http.security.HttpSecurity` CDI event:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `quarkus.http.auth.roles-mapping` property and the `rolesMapping` method are mutually exclusive, so use only one of them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Share permission checks across paths"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To apply a permission check to many paths without repeating it in every permission set, mark the permission as shared.\n"
"{project-name} always applies a shared permission when its path matches, in addition to the most specific unshared permission."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For unshared permission checks, only one path match is applied, the most specific one.\n"
"When a path matches as the most specific, you can specify multiple permissions for that path and they are all applied."
msgstr ""

msgid "The <<custom-http-security-policy,custom policy>> named `custom` is also applied on the `/admin/1` path, together with the `admin-policy1` policy."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, use a shared permission to map `SecurityIdentity` roles for a group of paths:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Role `root` will be able to access `/secured/user/\\*` and `/secured/admin/*` paths."
msgstr "ロール `root` は、 `/secured/user/\\*` および `/secured/admin/*` パスにアクセスできるようになります。"

msgid ""
"The `/secured/*` path can only be accessed by authenticated users.\n"
"This way, you have secured the `/secured/all` path and so on."
msgstr "`/secured/*` パスには、認証されたユーザーのみがアクセスできます。このようにして、 `/secured/all` パスなどが保護されます。"

msgid "Shared permissions are always applied before unshared ones, therefore a `SecurityIdentity` with the `root` role will have the `user` role as well."
msgstr "共有権限は常に非共有権限の前に適用されるため、 `root` ロールを持つ `SecurityIdentity` には `user` ロールも付与されます。"

msgid "Disable a permission"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To turn off a permission without deleting its configuration, set its `enabled` property to `false`.\n"
"The `enabled` property is runtime configuration, so you can turn the permission set back on without rebuilding the application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To turn the permission set back on at runtime, use a system property or environment variable, such as:\n"
"`-Dquarkus.http.auth.permission.permit1.enabled=true`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Authorize with security annotations"
msgstr ""

msgid "To keep each authorization rule next to the code that it protects, annotate Jakarta REST endpoints and CDI bean methods with security annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid "{project-name} includes built-in security to allow for link:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Role-based_access_control[Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)] based on the common security annotations `@RolesAllowed`, `@DenyAll`, and `@PermitAll`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Authorization checks for `quarkus.http.auth.` configurations are performed before security checks for standard security annotations.\n"
"Therefore, `@PermitAll` only permits access to paths that are not already restricted by HTTP permissions.\n"
"`@PermitAll` cannot override HTTP-level security configurations, only relax restrictions imposed by other standard security annotations such as `@RolesAllowed`."
msgstr "`quarkus.http.auth.` 設定の認可チェックは、標準セキュリティーアノテーションのセキュリティーチェックの前に実行されます。そのため、 `@PermitAll` は、HTTP 権限によってまだ制限されていないパスへのアクセスのみを許可します。 `@PermitAll` は HTTP レベルのセキュリティー設定をオーバーライドすることはできません。 `@RolesAllowed` などの他の標準セキュリティーアノテーションによって課せられた制限を緩和するだけです。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "Quarkus annotation types summary"
msgstr "Quarkus のアノテーション型の概要"

