msgid "Path-matching rules"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"{project-name} chooses the permission sets that apply to a request by comparing the request path and method with the `paths` and `methods` of each permission set.\n"
"When several match, the one with the most specific path wins."
msgstr ""

msgid "The rules in this section decide which path is the most specific."
msgstr ""

msgid "Paths and methods"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a path ends with the `*` wildcard, the query it generates matches all sub-paths.\n"
"Otherwise, it queries for an exact match and only matches that specific path:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `$$*$$` wildcard at the end of the path matches zero or more path segments, but never any word starting from the `/public` path.\n"
"For that reason, a path like `/public-info` is not matched by this pattern.\n"
"The `/public*` pattern is the same as the `/public/*` pattern."
msgstr ""

msgid "Requests with an unlisted method"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The request is rejected if it matches one or more permission sets based on the path but none of the required methods.\n"
"An anonymous request is rejected with the challenge of the configured authentication mechanism, for example, the HTTP 401 status for Basic authentication, and an authenticated request gets the HTTP 403 status.\n"
"When no authentication mechanism is active, the anonymous request also gets the HTTP 403 status."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For example, with the `permit1` permission set from <<matching-on-paths-and-methods>>, `GET /public/foo` matches both the path and method and is therefore allowed.\n"
"In contrast, `POST /public/foo` matches the path but not the method, and is therefore rejected."
msgstr ""

msgid "Longest path wins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Matching is always done on the \"longest path wins\" basis.\n"
"Less specific permission sets are not considered if a more specific one has been matched:"
msgstr ""
"マッチングは常に「最長パスが優先される」という基準で行われます。\n"
"具体的な権限セットがマッチした場合、それよりも具体性に欠ける権限セットは考慮されません。"

msgid ""
"With this configuration, `GET /public/forbidden-folder/foo` matches the paths of both permission sets.\n"
"However, because the longer path matches the path of the `deny1` permission set, `deny1` is chosen, and the request is rejected."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Subpath permissions precede root path permissions, as the `deny1` versus `permit1` permission example shows.\n"
"This rule also applies when a subpath permission allows access to a public resource while the root path permission requires authorization:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wildcards inside a path: longest path to the <code>*</code> wildcard wins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A path that ends with the `$$*$$` wildcard matches all sub-paths.\n"
"A trailing wildcard can follow other characters, but it still matches only whole path segments.\n"
"For example, `/three/fo$$*$$` is an alias for `/three/fo/$$*$$`, so it matches `/three/fo` and `/three/fo/bar`, but not `/three/foo`.\n"
"The wildcard can also be applied in the middle of a path, representing a single path segment.\n"
"An inner wildcard must occupy a whole segment, so path separators always enclose it, as seen in the `/public/$$*$$/about-us` path.\n"
"A path such as `/api/v$$*$$/detail` is not allowed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When several path patterns correspond to the same request path, the system selects the longest sub-path leading to the `$$*$$` wildcard.\n"
"In this context, every path segment character is more specific than the `$$*$$` wildcard."
msgstr ""
"複数のパスパターンが同じリクエストパスに対応する場合、システムは `$$*$$` ワイルドカードにつながる最長のサブパスを選択します。\n"
"この文脈では、すべてのパスセグメント文字は、 `$$*$$` ワイルドカード\n"
"よりも具体的になります。"

msgid "Here is a simple example:"
msgstr "簡単な例を挙げてみます。"

msgid "Request paths like `/api/product/detail` can only be accessed by authenticated users."
msgstr "`/api/product/detail` などのリクエストパスには、認証済みユーザーのみがアクセスできます。"

msgid "The path `/api/public-product/detail` is more specific, therefore accessible by anyone."
msgstr "パス `/api/public-product/detail` はより詳細であるため、どのユーザーもアクセスできます。"

msgid ""
"Test all paths that you secure with HTTP security policies.\n"
"Writing path patterns with multiple wildcards can be cumbersome, so make sure that each path is authorized as you intend."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the following example, paths are ordered from the most specific to the least specific one:"
msgstr "次の例では、パスは最も詳細なものから最も詳細でないものの順に並べられています。"

msgid ""
"The `$$*$$` wildcard at the end of the path matches zero or more path segments.\n"
"The `$$*$$` wildcard placed anywhere else matches exactly one path segment."
msgstr ""
"パスの末尾にある `$$*$$` ワイルドカードは、0 個以上のパスセグメントにマッチします。\n"
"他の場所に配置された `$$*$$` ワイルドカードは、1 つのパスセグメントのみにマッチします。"

msgid "Most specific method wins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a path is registered with multiple permission sets, the permission sets explicitly specifying an HTTP method that matches the request take precedence.\n"
"In this instance, the permission sets without methods only come into effect if the request method does not match permission sets with the method specification."
msgstr ""
"パスが複数の権限セットに登録されている場合、リクエストにマッチする HTTP メソッドを明示的に指定する権限セットが優先されます。\n"
"この場合、メソッドのない権限セットは、リクエストメソッドがメソッド仕様を持つ権限セットとマッチしない場合にのみ、有効になります。"

msgid ""
"With this configuration, `GET /public/foo` matches the paths of both permission sets.\n"
"However, it specifically aligns with the explicit method of the `permit1` permission set.\n"
"Therefore, `permit1` is selected, and the request is accepted."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In contrast, `PUT /public/foo` does not match the method permissions of `permit1`.\n"
"As a result, `deny1` is activated, leading to the rejection of the request."
msgstr "一方、 `PUT/public/foo` は `permit1` のメソッド権限とマッチしません。その結果、 `deny1` がアクティブになり、リクエストが拒否されます。"

msgid "Several winning permission sets: all must permit"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sometimes, these rules allow multiple permission sets to win simultaneously.\n"
"In that case, for the request to proceed, all the permissions must allow access.\n"
"For this to happen, both must either have specified the method or have no method.\n"
"Method-specific matches take precedence."
msgstr ""

msgid "With this configuration, `GET /api/foo` matches the paths of both permission sets, so it requires both the `user` and `admin` roles."
msgstr ""

msgid "Permission paths and HTTP root path"
msgstr "権限パスとHTTPルートパス"

msgid "The `quarkus.http.root-path` configuration property changes the xref:http-reference.adoc#context-path[http endpoint context path]."
msgstr "`quarkus.http.root-path` 設定プロパティは、 xref:http-reference.adoc#context-path[http endpoint context path] を変更します。"

msgid "By default, `quarkus.http.root-path` is prepended automatically to configured permission paths that do not start with a forward slash, for example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This configuration is equivalent to the following:"
msgstr "この構成は以下に相当します。 :"

msgid ""
"A leading slash changes how the configured permission path is interpreted.\n"
"The configured URL is used as-is, and paths are not adjusted if the value of `quarkus.http.root-path` changes."
msgstr ""
"先頭のスラッシュは、設定された権限パスの解釈方法を変更します。\n"
"設定された URL はそのまま使用され、 `quarkus.http.root-path` の値が変更されてもパスは調整されません。"

msgid "This configuration only impacts resources served from the fixed or static URL, `/public`, which might not match your application resources if `quarkus.http.root-path` has been set to something other than `/`."
msgstr "この設定は、固定または静的 URL `/public` から提供されるリソースにのみ影響します。この URL は、 `quarkus.http.root-path` が `/` 以外に設定されていると、アプリケーションリソースとマッチしない可能性があります。"

msgid "For more information, see link:https://quarkus.io/blog/path-resolution-in-quarkus/[Path Resolution in Quarkus]."
msgstr "詳細は、link:https://quarkus.io/blog/path-resolution-in-quarkus/[Path Resolution in Quarkus] を参照してください。"

msgid "Set up path-specific authorization programmatically"
msgstr "パス固有の認可をプログラムで設定します"

msgid ""
"To set up path rules in code, for example, from configuration values that your code reads, observe the `io.quarkus.vertx.http.security.HttpSecurity` CDI event.\n"
"{project-name} fires this event when the runtime configuration is ready."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also configure the authorization policies from <<authorization-using-configuration>> programmatically.\n"
"For example, consider this configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The same authorization policies can be configured programmatically:"
msgstr "同じ認可ポリシーをプログラムで設定できます。"

msgid "The `HttpSecurity` CDI event can also select the authentication mechanism and the policy for each path:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Register the Basic and form-based authentication mechanisms, so that the paths in this example can select them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the Basic authentication and authorize the requests with your own `io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.security.HttpSecurityPolicy`, such as the `CustomNamedHttpSecPolicy` bean from <<custom-http-security-policy>>.\n"
"A policy that is a CDI bean without a name is also a global policy.\n"
"To apply a policy only to this path, give the bean a name, as `CustomNamedHttpSecPolicy` does, or do not declare the class as a CDI bean and pass an instance created with `new`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the Bearer token authentication and authorize the `SecurityIdentity` with your own policy.\n"
"Bearer token authentication requires the `quarkus-oidc`, `quarkus-smallrye-jwt`, or `quarkus-elytron-security-oauth2` extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use Authorization Code Flow mechanism, which requires the `quarkus-oidc` extension, and write your own policy based on incoming request headers.\n"
"A policy with this signature also runs for anonymous requests, so it checks for them first."
msgstr ""

msgid "When Quarkus fires the `HttpSecurity` CDI event, the runtime configuration is ready, so you can inject configuration properties."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Require that all the requests to the `/user-info` path have string permissions `openid`, `email` and `profile`.\n"
"The same authorization can be required with the `@PermissionsAllowed(value = { \"openid\", \"email\", \"profile\" }, inclusive = true)` annotation instance placed on an endpoint."
msgstr "`/user-info` パスへのすべてのリクエストに、文字列権限 `openid` 、 `email` 、 `profile` があることを要求します。同じ認可は、エンドポイントに配置された `@PermissionsAllowed(value = { \"openid\", \"email\", \"profile\" }, inclusive = true)` アノテーションインスタンスで要求できます。"

msgid ""
"When permissions from the `application.properties` file and from the `HttpSecurity` event match the same request, the <<path-matching-rules,path-matching rules>> decide between them: the more specific permission wins, whether it has the longer path or lists the request method.\n"
"Both permissions apply only when they are equally specific, as described in <<matching-multiple-paths-and-methods-both-win>>, or when one of them is a <<shared-permission-checks,shared permission>>.\n"
"Programmatic setup for the management interface is not supported."
msgstr ""

